// @run
// @log zz
// @log 1
// THE NEIGHBOURING POSITION whose key the SPELLING cannot answer: the list-typed
// inline-shape field whose ELEMENT is a declared map ALIAS (`{m: M[]}`).
//
// The field's own text is `M[]`, so every name-side key test on it is false —
// `nameIsI32KeyedMap` reads the `{[K]:` prefix and `M[]` has none. What answers is the
// element INTERN, which classifies `M[]`'s element through the same ref-list kind ladder
// every other element takes and reaches the map arm on the RESOLVED type; the flag is then
// asked of the element name the intern already holds.
//
// A declared ALIAS is not a second source of the flag the way a declared STRUCT type is: a
// `type S = {m: {[i32]: V}[]}`'s FIELD annotation is its own map-array `TypeRef`, but a
// `type M = {[i32]: V}` alias's RHS is not one the arena scan's bare-map arm claims, so
// with the fix reverted this spelling emits invalid wasm at `vl check` rc 0 exactly as the
// spelled-out one does.
//
// The value is `string` — an mv-SLOT value, so the failure mode is the silent one.

type M = {[i32]: string}

const s: {m: M[]} = { m: [Map()] }
s.m[0][11] = "zz"
print(s.m[0][11] ?? "-") // zz
print(s.m[0].size)       // 1
